  "notes": "Penn State Erie, The Behrend College. Pattern B (genuinely separate curriculum from University Park's BIOL-2022.json). Sourced via bulletin_scraper.py from 2022-2023 archive. Differs from 2026: Semester 3 offers CHEM 210 path (with option for Gen Ed instead); Semesters 5-6 offer physics path alternates (PHYS 211 instead of 250; PHYS 212 instead of 251), and Semester 5 allows CHEM 203 or Gen Ed. These reflect the different organic chemistry and physics pathway options available in 2022 versus 2026's prescribed path specification. QA correction (2026-09-17): Semester 4's CAS 100 item was originally modeled as a generic slot on the claim that '(code not linked in bulletin)' -- a fresh bulletin_scraper.py run against the real 2022-2023 archive shows this is false: the 2022 bulletin's own HTML links 'CAS 100' as a real <a> tag (is_generic_slot=False), it's simply a stale code no longer in the modern catalog (CAS split it into 100A/100B/100C). Resolved to a course item with options CAS 100A/CAS 100B/CAS 100C, matching the identical fix already applied to BUSECONBH-2022 and CHEMBH-2022 for the same stale code in the same catalog year. QA fix (2026-09-17): added explicit MATH 3/4/21/22 items (Semester 1: MATH 3/4; Semester 2: MATH 21/22) -- CHEM 110's real prereq is MATH 22, which chains through MATH 21/4/3, none of which this year's bulletin suggested-plan lists (PSU's plans assume calculus-ready students); this is the same real prereq-chain fix already applied to BIOLBH-2026.json, applied here for self-verification parity. Self-verification before fix: 'Could not schedule remaining requirements' for CHEM 110/111/BIOL 240W/CHEM 112/113/210/STAT 250/CHEM 202-203 (or 203 for 2024/2025). After fix: 0 warnings.",
